      "id": 1,
      "text": "Fort Bellefontaine was erected in the winter of 1805 by Colonel Jacob Kingsbury, complete with log cabins, a trading house, bakery, blacksmith shop, and huts for soldiers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bellefontaine_Neighbors%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1834 the fort was abandoned and the surrounding land was parceled into public land grants.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bellefontaine_Neighbors%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s name derives from a clear‑water spring called “la belle fontaine” that early French settlers noted near the river.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bellefontaine_Neighbors%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "General Daniel Bissell, the fort’s commander, later owned land here and his house is listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
